<span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T08:30:54-07:00","id":665778,"title":"","content":"Hey cool, I saw those on Deviantart a while back. I really like them, and the others you had there.<br /> <br /> I guess one thing to note about the forms is their sizes. The specific differences between them are given in the Forms section of the book, for instance Gauru is supposed to be one and a half times their Hishu height, and weigh almost four times as much. During first edition everyone seemed on a different page regarding the forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-15-2015, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T08:40:02-07:00","id":665790,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Storm Lord there is a bit on the skinny side. The description in second edition says a gauru form werewolf has &quot;arms the size of most people's waists&quot; and &quot;legs like tree trunks&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically hulk-shaped is more the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T10:42:14-07:00","id":665861,"title":"","content":"Dunno, Rachel Snow is the head of a military contract enterprise. I don't see her wearing belly showing outfits. Nevermind how Storm-Lordy she is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T10:53:00-07:00","id":665892,"title":"","content":"There's a couple pictures of her in the Hunting Grounds: The Rockies, book, where she's wearing similar outfit. In the first her midriff is covered but she's wearing a thick collar, and the picture of her with her full pack does depict her with bared midriff. She likes her belt buckles, too, apparently.<br /> <br /> Max Roman is more of the suit-and-tie type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:48:03-07:00","id":665945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/665703-artwork-suggestions-and-feedback?p=665790#post665790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Storm Lord there is a bit on the skinny side. The description in second edition says a gauru form werewolf has &quot;arms the size of most people's waists&quot; and &quot;legs like tree trunks&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically hulk-shaped is more the norm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just re-interpreted the character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> thanks all!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:02:52-07:00","id":665953,"title":"","content":"I really like the soft color pallette and warm color tones you use for both the backgrounds and characters. Normally WoD art tends toward the high contrast styles but this really works to convey a sense that the wolves in the background and the person in the foreground are one and the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:45:43-07:00","id":665993,"title":"","content":"Personally I would like more artwork depicting the Urshal (near wolf) form, as that is bound to be the one used most for hunting and everything short of end of the world combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:21:25-07:00","id":666030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/665703-artwork-suggestions-and-feedback?p=665993#post665993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would like more artwork depicting the Urshal (near wolf) form, as that is bound to be the one used most for hunting and everything short of end of the world combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>the examples are just some of my fan-artwork.<br /> I don't know If I will have to paint other forms.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:40:38-07:00","id":667120,"title":"","content":"Hey, I made this account just to comment on your art. I liked it since I first saw it on deviantart, you have pretty distinctive &quot;bright&quot; artstyle that is quite different and refreshing to look at. I have 2 suggestions: first, try to make scenes a bit less static - in your pieces there's not much motion, but still, werewolf is all about that. Light sources exploding, shadows having sharp edges, &quot;running out&quot; of the light, hair being more unkempt, dirt, some facial imperfections, cloth folded in places to suggest that character moved recently or is about to jump out etc.<br /> <br /> And second is just a part of wishlist - personally what I would like to see is more alternative depictions of Gauru form - burly, big wolves are always fine, though it's not said I wouldn't welcome very tall, thin, &quot;sharp&quot; looking Bone Shadows, similar a bit to the depictions of hungry Wendigo from american legends.<br /> <br /> In W:tF 1st ed Appearences part under tribe description would help imagine them. Always remember that Uratha are &quot;half-spirit, half-men&quot;, so lots of things around them work on kinda symbolic logic. Same with transformation: low-Harmony werewolf transforms constantly instinctively, often not even noticing it, having &quot;fluid&quot; appearance. I can even imagine that forms he is taking look different when circumstances are: when he is particularly hungry or going for the flesh of humans, he might have bigger jaw in Urshul and teeth looking like shark ones, that is like three rows of needless. On the other hand, while interacting with human or wolf-blooded ally in the pack, he might have blunter teeth or look more canine, maybe like caucasian shepherd or akbash dog or one of those attack dogs like canarian one. <br /> <br /> Anyway, cheers, enjoy the ride and get paid good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:51:52-07:00","id":667207,"title":"","content":"I love your &quot;warm&quot; art - they are great, adding a bit life to normal artwork of gamelines. I can clearly say I'm looking forward to see your's arts in both <b>Mage</b> 2ED and in <b>Pack</b> books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:15:56-07:00","id":667276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/665703-artwork-suggestions-and-feedback?p=665892#post665892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a couple pictures of her in the Hunting Grounds: The Rockies, book, where she's wearing similar outfit. In the first her midriff is covered but she's wearing a thick collar, and the picture of her with her full pack does depict her with bared midriff. She likes her belt buckles, too, apparently.<br /> <br /> Max Roman is more of the suit-and-tie type.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd think she would favor stuff like Kevlar, if only because she actually produces that shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:29:22-07:00","id":667289,"title":"","content":"Some people take, 'Allow No One to Witness or Tend Your Weakness,' very seriously. And she seems to be descended from a more traditionalist bent, representing the more standard depiction of werewolves in games, I think, opposite Max Roman. Still, I think it's fair to assume most of the standard werewolf antagonists won't be using bullets. The fiction does give an example of vampires firing at the Black Moon eXtreme with silver bullets but the BMX were sort of asking for it, being vampire hunters and all.<br /> <br /> The Calm Before the Storm pack, from the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/63514/ReadyMade-Player-Characters-Werewolf-The-Forsaken\" target=\"_blank\">premade characters booklet</a>, take the more tactical bent.<br /> <br /> Rachel snow showed up in one of my games, she was sort of an ally to a member of our pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-16-2015, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:16:56-07:00","id":667986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miriander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/665703-artwork-suggestions-and-feedback?p=667120#post667120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I made this account just to comment on your art. I liked it since I first saw it on deviantart, you have pretty distinctive &quot;bright&quot; artstyle that is quite different and refreshing to look at. I have 2 suggestions: first, try to make scenes a bit less static - in your pieces there's not much motion, but still, werewolf is all about that. Light sources exploding, shadows having sharp edges, &quot;running out&quot; of the light, hair being more unkempt, dirt, some facial imperfections, cloth folded in places to suggest that character moved recently or is about to jump out etc.<br /> <br /> And second is just a part of wishlist - personally what I would like to see is more alternative depictions of Gauru form - burly, big wolves are always fine, though it's not said I wouldn't welcome very tall, thin, &quot;sharp&quot; looking Bone Shadows, similar a bit to the depictions of hungry Wendigo from american legends.<br /> <br /> In W:tF 1st ed Appearences part under tribe description would help imagine them. Always remember that Uratha are &quot;half-spirit, half-men&quot;, so lots of things around them work on kinda symbolic logic. Same with transformation: low-Harmony werewolf transforms constantly instinctively, often not even noticing it, having &quot;fluid&quot; appearance. I can even imagine that forms he is taking look different when circumstances are: when he is particularly hungry or going for the flesh of humans, he might have bigger jaw in Urshul and teeth looking like shark ones, that is like three rows of needless. On the other hand, while interacting with human or wolf-blooded ally in the pack, he might have blunter teeth or look more canine, maybe like caucasian shepherd or akbash dog or one of those attack dogs like canarian one.<br /> <br /> Anyway, cheers, enjoy the ride and get paid good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you <u><i>very</i></u> much and welcome to the forum.<br /> Nice idea about the alternative depictions of the gauru form!<br /> About the motion: keep in mind that the pieces here and on deviantart are all concept-art, focused on the mood not on the motion: you will see a couple of my artwork in W20 shattere dreams really <i>full </i>of dynamism. Mood is very important to me: on the firs art I favored red and orange, brown and yellow to depict the red talon concept. In the second pict more fair colors, like shiny grey/blue and fair yellow for the bone shadows and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:24:56-07:00","id":671981,"title":"","content":"Saw your art posted on Tumblr a few times! I love it! I think their outfits look fantastic, and I love the bright, fresh color of your work. Reminds me a bit of some comic book artists which is definitely NOT a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to seeing your work in some OP books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T23:45:55-07:00","id":680695,"title":"","content":"Friggin' sweet! May I ask what your username is on Deviantart and Tumblr?<br /> <br /> As for suggestions, I second the idea of more varied looks for Gauru and the other forms. Some might look Strix-like, all pitch black. billowing smoke, silent feet and glowing eyes. Others have such boiling blood that even their flesh and fur take on a reddish tint, and bony protrusions come out of their spine, elbows and such. A particularly tech-loving Iron Master might even ask spirits of technology to inhabit fetishes bound into his flesh that come out in certain forms, giving him a cyborg look.<br /> <br /> I'd love it if you drew a Ghost Wolf in Gauru form whose Harmony is so deep into the Spirit side that he looks like an abstraction of a werewolf, more of a humanoid, muscular, crimson whirlwind of predatory features. If you would like a reference, look for fan art of the shoggoths from the Cthulhu Mythos, but still roughly human-shaped and wolf-like. He might even be mistaken for an Idigam that hasn't coalesced yet at first sight. Some kind of boogeyman the Tribes tell stories about to warn new Uratha about the dangers of losing oneself to the spirit side. It would be even cooler to have this boogeyman showing up inside the smoke flowing upwards from a bonfire with werewolves gathered around it. I don't know if that would be too hard to draw, so I apologize if it is a tall order.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, how do you envision Spirits and the Shadow Realm as a whole, in visual terms? I like to use the <a href=\"http://i39.tinypic.com/5f3mg4.png\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Noise from &quot;The World Ends With You&quot;</b></a> and the <a href=\"http://www.thebbps.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2006/09/wp04_1600.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>painterly aesthetic from &quot;Okami&quot;</b></a> as inspiration. I usually imagine the Shadow in tones of sepia and red, with more nuanced palettes showing up in locations and denizens of distinction. As an extension of that, the unclean hybridization of the magath is reflected in their garish and psychedelic combinations of colors. If a magath starts looking like something from an acid trip seen through a rainbow filter, it is probably very bizarre in Influences and behavior.<br /> <br /> Do you have any headcanons for what Father Wolf and Mother Luna might have looked like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T15:09:54-07:00","id":681435,"title":"","content":"I think something I would love to see in your imagery, would be the manifestation of spirit brands. Maybe with onyx paths blessing you can head something like the runes from apocalypse as spirit brands in forsaken. I imagine each gift has its own brand appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T04:28:04-08:00","id":746362,"title":"","content":"That's actually great arts, but I don't know why, I've always seen the Gauru are monstrously muscular... Even when it made no sense compared to the frame of the human form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 11-01-2015, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123