lue":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:42:55-08:00","id":751594,"title":"","content":"I think the girls is mostly due to her curling up pose, but I like it. Nudity is always a plus for me, though not everyone feels the same way.<br /> <br /> Really dig the Ivory Claw, though, I feel like they should always be sharp dressers, or at least stand out in any crowd they're a part of, providing they're not hiding. Also like the yellow eyes, though my own characters are black, at least in the more wolvish forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T13:31:32-08:00","id":759276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/665703-artwork-suggestions-and-feedback?p=750912#post750912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks all for your suggestions.<br /> Yes, it's not simple to portrait a gauru form like an enormous muscular killing machine for a lot of reason: Apocalypse of course, have had a great influence in almost every werewolf-bipedal adaptation, and I'm largely influnced by Abrar and Araya. I personally like the ''savage horror'', so, If I can hide something about the gauru, I do it, like put them in the background, or not show the whole body.<br /> I want them like horror.-hunter, not nature-warrior.<br /> By the way, If I will have to interpretate a couple of gauru form for The pack, I'll gladly follow your taste.<br /> So, thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here two other pieces.<br /> One from apocalypse, the other well, the new Ivory Claws are scarier than the 1st edition. I like them.<br /> Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-mxp1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xtp1/v/t1.0-9/12196081_1699975200233760_8231789295390324781_n.jpg?oh=9e43c0331921f52b0b670e65404d4053&amp;oe=56C05AA0\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think your garou look too....soft, i think that the word. Like the cover of <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/3373.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/3373.jpg</a> that, sorry not good IMO.<br /> <br /> While i get what you going for not showing the whole body and not trying to do apocalypse`s wolf-barbarians thing what you do show should be more savage and less tame. Less lean and soft and more feral.<br /> <br /> The one im quoting though, is more of what i am talking about. (The one of the left) but for what i have seen you should try more body types than &quot;perfectly lean&quot; maybe bulky and muscular or somwhat fat and muscle. Just my 2 cents.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T09:33:50-08: